/* The tree f a b is accepted from q0 only through the second transition for
   (q0, f): the first puts the child a in q1, which has no transition on a.
   A checker that searches for a counterexample along the first transition
   alone reports one here, although the property holds. */
%BEGING
S -> f a b.
%ENDG

%BEGINA
q0 f -> q1 q2.
q0 f -> q2 q1.
q1 b -> .
q2 a -> .
%ENDA
